<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#mapping_2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visual entity 'man' wearing a white head covering and traditional garment is mapped onto the textual stereotype 'stereotype_muslims_sex_with_animals'. The text's suggestion of 'let's try a goat' combined with the visual marker (head covering) creates an analogical mapping where the man's appearance is used to represent a harmful stereotype — that Muslim men are associated with sexual behavior involving animals. This is an implicit mapping between the visual marker and the textual stereotype."@en .
