<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#concept_periods> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text references 'your habibi is on periods', which refers to the biological process of menstruation. This concept is not visible in the image but is essential to understanding the scenario being described. It is a sensitive topic that the meme trivializes for comedic effect, which is part of its offensive nature."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scene"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#contextuallyReferentAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semanticallyAdjacentTo> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#stereotype_muslims_sex_with_animals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This stereotype is implicitly referenced in the meme through the visual of the man in traditional attire (head covering, robe) combined with the text suggesting a crude, animalistic solution ('let's try a goat') to a sexual frustration. The combination of the visual marker (head covering) and the text creates a harmful stereotype that associates Muslim men with sexual behavior involving animals, which is a widely recognized and offensive trope in some contexts."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metadata"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#SemioticProjection> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TemplateStructure> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Template Structure elements from the image. Template Structure includes: template patterns, organizational frameworks, structural elements, layout templates, framework components, and structural patterns. For each structural element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'contrast_template', 'layout_framework'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the contrast template', 'the layout framework'), 3) A brief description of the structural pattern or framework. Focus on the underlying organizational structure of the meme. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"contrast_template\", \"label\": \"the contrast template\", \"description\": \"The meme follows a contrast template with calm foreground subject against chaotic background scene\"}"@en .
