<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'when you're feeling horny asf...' uses the second-person pronoun 'you', directly addressing the viewer/user. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is mapped onto the visual entity 'man', who is depicted as the person experiencing the described scenario. The user is projected onto the man as 'you' — the subject of the text's narrative — making the man a visual representation of the user's own potential experience or a humorous stand-in for the user's situation. The man's gesture and expression reinforce this projection by embodying the 'resignation' or 'humorous acceptance' of the absurd solution."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#comparativelyPositionedTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
