<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#OverallIntent> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Overall Intent elements from the image. Overall Intent includes: communicative purposes, creator intentions, message goals, intended effects, purpose indicators, and intent signals. For each intentional element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'humor_intent', 'social_commentary'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the humor intent', 'the social commentary'), 3) A brief description of the intended purpose or effect. Focus on what the meme creator likely intended to communicate or achieve. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"humor_intent\", \"label\": \"the humor intent\", \"description\": \"The meme appears designed to create humor through the contrast between the girl's calm expression and the chaotic fire scene\"}"@en .
