<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VerbalIrony> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text saying the opposite of another dimension in memes, e.g. contradicting visual reality"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#term_asf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The term 'asf' is a slang expression used in the text to intensify the feeling of being 'horny'. This slang is not visible in the image and requires knowledge of internet slang and informal language to understand the level of intensity being conveyed. It adds to the crude, humorous tone of the meme."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#man_gesturing_with_open_hands> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A man in traditional attire with a head covering is smiling broadly and gesturing with both hands open, palms facing forward. The gesture suggests openness, surrender, or a humorous resignation, fitting the meme's context of absurd humor."@en .
