<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundKnowledge> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Background Knowledge elements from the image. Background Knowledge includes: cultural references, historical context, social knowledge, domain-specific information, contextual cues, and background information. For each knowledge element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'cultural_reference', 'historical_context'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the cultural reference', 'the historical context'), 3) A brief description of the knowledge or context required to understand the element. Focus on information that viewers need to know to fully comprehend the meme. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"cultural_reference\", \"label\": \"the cultural reference\", \"description\": \"Reference to the 'This is fine' dog meme, requiring knowledge of internet culture to understand the irony\"}"@en .
