_:n7a2a2d5a70744cec9275b2e2bd998220b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#humor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The man's broad smile and open-handed gesture convey a lighthearted, joking demeanor, fitting the absurd and crude humor of the meme's text. His expression suggests amusement or mock resignation to the ridiculous situation described."@en .
_:n7a2a2d5a70744cec9275b2e2bd998220b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#audience_id_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for an internet-savvy audience familiar with crude humor, shock value, and internet slang (e.g., 'asf'). The target community likely includes users who appreciate absurdist, sexually suggestive, and taboo-breaking humor, often found on social media platforms like Reddit, Twitter, or meme sites. The audience is expected to understand the crude nature of the text and the visual stereotype, and to find the juxtaposition of the man's traditional attire with the absurd solution ('let's try a goat') funny, even if offensive."@en .
